  "prompt": "Nested env var is not JSON-decoded when a dict field's value type contains another dict\n\nExample: \n\n```py\nimport os\n\nfrom pydantic_settings import BaseSettings, SettingsConfigDict\n\n\nclass Settings(BaseSettings):\n    model_config = SettingsConfigDict(env_prefix=\"APP_\", env_nested_delimiter=\"__\")\n\n    a: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\n    b: dict[str, list[dict[str, str]]] = {}\n\n\nos.environ[\"APP_A__X\"] = '[\"v\"]'\nos.environ[\"APP_B__X\"] = '[{\"k\": \"v\"}]'\n\nSettings()\n# a.x == ['v']\n# b.x: ValidationError, input_value='[{\"k\": \"v\"}]' (str), expected list\n```\n\nThe bug is in [`EnvSettingsSource.next_field`](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/blob/e9588aefb8a2fafa7fe7868a5aa54f24458b7497/pydantic_settings/sources/providers/env.py#L277-L284), the outer annotation for `dict` has to be checked before recursing into its type arguments.",
